{
    "$comment": "The catalogue of every command the addon answers, and the addon method that answers it. Hand-written: this is the specification. `scripts/generate-command-surface.mjs` emits the addon's dispatch table, its runtime routing list and the renderer's command names from it, so a command that is not here is unreachable and unspellable. Which of these mutate the edited scene is request.schema.json's to say, and only its.",
    "$runtimeComment": "The commands the addon hands to the running game rather than answering itself. They are listed apart because they have no handler method: `_handle_runtime_request` routes each one, some to the game over the debugger bridge and some to the editor. Before they were listed here the addon carried them twice — once to decide what to route and once to route it — and neither list was reconciled with anything.",
    "runtimeCommands": [
        "runtime.run",
        "runtime.stop",
        "runtime.restart",
        "runtime.get_state",
        "runtime.get_tree",
        "runtime.inspect_node",
        "runtime.input",
        "runtime.capture",
        "runtime.get_monitors",
        "runtime.wait"
    ],
